  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AMA-ProjectdeliveryFoodAssist&amp;Protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam and its partner (AMA) propose to support the response to food insecurity induced by the El Nin&#xf5; Phenomenon and the conflict, through Food Assistance and awareness sessions on safe programming and protection risks for 100 families in Montepuez District, CaboDelgado Province, Northern Mozambique.
The Mozambican non-governmental organization &#x201c;AMA&#x201d; &#x2013; Associa&#xe7;&#xe3;o Ambientalista &#x2013; is a grassroots organization based in Cabo Delgado, northern Mozambique and was created in 1990 in Pemba City, Province of Cabo Delgado, by a group of young people motivated by an interest in safeguarding of natural resources.
AMA has been growing, developing and establishingitself as a reference player in raising awareness and strengthening communities around the management of natural resources and the environment. The AMA team, made up of more than seventy members and more than fifty workers, designs and implements different activities, projects and other interventions in its strategic areas of development and the humanitarian sector in different districts of the Province of Cabo Delgado, located in the North region of Mozambique.
AMA is a relevant actor due to its long history and partnership in defending the tariff use of the benefits of Extractive Industries, arising from gas exploration in Cabo Delgado. AMA is also a leading actor for its intervention during the resettlement of evicted people around the LNG plant in the Palma District.
AMA&apos;s intervention in this project will focus on food assistance and protection, especially the distribution of food kits and raising awareness about safe programming and protection risks for people affected by conflict and food insecurity in the resettlement centers of Administrative Post of Montepuez City, to respond to the multi-faceted and cascading impacts of El Ni&#xf1;o-induced drought and floods, and conflict, which have affected several sectors, including agriculture, livelihoods and food security, etc.. In-kind food assistancewill be provided during three (3) months of project implementation. Food purchases will be made locally and will consist of rice, corn flour, beans, cooking oil, sugar and salt. The rations will be in accordance with WFP and Food Security Cluster standards. Before the food is distributed, people will benefit from awareness sessions on safe programming and protection risks.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AMA was original created in May 19, 1990 in the City of Pemba, Province of Cabo Delgado with the name of NUMA (Nucleus of the Environment) and was recognized and authorized to work by the Governor of the Province on January 31, 1991. In 2001 Its was registered asAMA - Associac&#xe3;o do Meio Ambiente  .   It is registered in the Bulletin of the Republic No 20, Series III , 16 May 2007.

AMA main objective is to protect the Environment thorough the sustainable use of natural resources (including extractive resources)  for the well being of communities. AMA uses massive education and promotes the inclusion of communities in the decision making process related to improving their lives.
For the project partnership with OXFAM, AMA will work in the community rights related to the exploitation of natural resources in the district of Palma  and Nhamanumbir , in Cabo Delgado .</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Associac&#xe3;o do Meio Ambiente</narrative>
